5\\u20132.0 dB** (slightly less than the full cut because the band energy is averaged across the full 250\\u2013500 Hz range, not just 300 Hz). The low band (60\\u2013250 Hz) may dip very slightly (~0.3 dB) at its top edge.\\n\\n---\\n\\nNow: snapshot \\u2192 apply \\u2192 re-render.\\n\\n## 2026-04-23 21:24 UTC\\n- Deepened built-in EQ band 1 on track 14 \\"koto thing\\": 308 Hz from -1.98 dB \\u2192 -4.0 dB (added -2 dB, Q\\u22480.55/bandwidth). Track 14 low_mid: 99.9 \\u2192 99.3 (\\u22120.6). Master low_mid: 99.9 \\u2192 99.2 (\\u22120.7). Master LUFS: -24.4 \\u2192 -24.6. Change kept.\\n\\n## 2026-04-23 21:34 UTC\\n- Track 14 \\"koto thing\\" built-in EQ band 1: -3.0 dB @ 287 Hz, bandwidth\\u22480.35 (Q\\u22481.5). Previous state was -4.0 dB @ 308 Hz. Stem low_mid: 99.3 \\u2192 98.5 (-0.8 dB). Master LUFS: -24.6 \\u2192 -24.9. True peak: -9.4 \\u2192 -10.1 dB. Note: built-in EQ coarse resolution landed -3 dB/287 Hz instead of requested -2 dB/300 Hz \\u2014 recommend Pro-Q 3 for precision on this track.\\n\\n## 2026-04-23 21:39 UTC\\n[Auto-saved on disconnect \\u2014 last agent response:]\\n\\n**Summary:** The -3 dB cut at 287 Hz on \\"koto thing\\" trimmed **-0.8 dB low_mid** and **-1.8 dB low** on the stem \\u2014 slightly asymmetric because 287 Hz sits right on the low/low_mid boundary. Master moved from **-24.6 \\u2192 -24.9 LUFS** and true peak dropped **0.7 dB**, giving a little more headroom.\\n\\n**One caveat to flag:** The built-in EQ\'s normalized gain scale resolved to **-3.0 dB @ 287 Hz** rather than exactly -2 dB @ 300 Hz. If you need exact values (or want the -2 dB you asked for), adding **Pro-Q 3** to this track would give you surgical Hz/dB precision. Want me to walk you through that, or are you happy with where it landed?\\n\\n## 2026-04-23 21:41 UTC\\nCut additional -2 dB at ~296 Hz (built-in EQ band 1, Q\\u22481.5) on track 14 \\"koto thing\\" \\u2014 total band now -5.15 dB. Low-mid: 98.5 \\u2192 96.8 (\\u22121.7 pts), LUFS: \\u221224.9 \\u21