19:31:25 [DEBUG] anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8cb352dc-5203-4436-bac4-57d37aa7b52e', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Full-stack smoke test. I just dropped two files into chat — the first one\'s a stem from FL, the second one\'s a song I want as a sonic reference. (1) Confirm where each\n  ▎ landed via get_workspace_status. If the stem is in drops/ instead of stems/, walk me through the Move-menu fix in the sidebar. (2) Render the full project with\n  ▎ prepare_batch_render so we have current numbers — read me the Ctrl+R instruction verbatim before waiting. After the export, run compare_to_reference between the master\n  ▎ and the reference file. (3) Pick the single biggest spectral problem the comparison surfaces and propose a concrete fix using the right tool: set_proq3 if Pro-Q 3 is\n  ▎ loaded, set_builtin_eq otherwise. Snapshot, predict the spectral_balance delta, apply, re-render the affected track + master, and report before/after as a table. (4) Now\n  ▎ load Fruity Compressor on the drum bus if it\'s not already there, and use set_compressor to add gentle bus compression — threshold around -12 dB, ratio 2:1, attack 10 ms,\n  ▎  release 80 ms, +1 dB makeup. After it\'s set, right-click each Fruity Comp knob in FL → "edit value", read me the actual displayed values, and tell me which axes drift\n  ▎ more than 20% from what you intended. (5) Sidechain the bass to the kick: pre-load Fruity Compressor on bass, call apply_sidechain, read me the dropdown advisory\n  ▎ verbatim, and pause for me to confirm in FL. After I confirm, tune the bass comp\'s threshold/release for ~6 dB pump and re-render. (6) When everything\'s done,\n  ▎ write_history_entry summarising all four moves with their numeric deltas.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'con