 3 | [808] choucroute | -16.6 | -5.6 dB | 206 Hz | Loud, full-range 808, lots of low-mid/mid |\\n| 4 | JP - Simmie Hat | -34.9 | -15.2 dB | 10.2 kHz | Air-heavy, fine |\\n| 5 | JP - Low Hat | -37.6 | -22.1 dB | 3.7 kHz | Quiet, OK |\\n| 6 | JP - Crack Hat | -30.5 | -14.5 dB | 5.6 kHz | Fine |\\n| 7 | JP - Greek Clap | -28.5 | -10.9 dB | 4.0 kHz | Good body+air balance |\\n| 8 | JP - Metal Clap | -25.9 | -10.4 dB | 5.2 kHz | Decent, slight low-mid weight |\\n| 9 | JP - Bongo Perc | -22.8 | -4.5 dB | 1.5 kHz | Hot true peak; very low-mid/mid heavy |\\n| 10 | Nuclear Kick | -11.0 | -4.0 dB | 371 Hz | Extremely loud; dominant sub/low |\\n| 14 | koto thing | -24.1 | -8.6 dB | 2.2 kHz | Low-mid/mid heavy; potential mud with 808 |\\n| 15 | koto thing #2 | -36.3 | -23.0 dB | 3.8 kHz | Quiet, OK |\\n| 16 | Cymatics Reverse Air | -29.3 | -13.3 dB | 4.1 kHz | Low-mid spike (71.6) vs. clean sub |\\n| 17 | Goalbz Tag | -23.3 | -11.3 dB | 2.4 kHz | Mid-focused, no sub (intentional tag) |\\n\\n**Key issues identified:**\\n1. **Master true peak = 0.0 dBTP** \\u2014 clipping/limiting at ceiling. No headroom.\\n2. **Nuclear Kick (10)** at -11 LUFS is far too loud relative to the mix \\u2014 dominant driver of clipping.\\n3. **808 (3)** at -16.6 LUFS is very hot and full-range (sub through air), likely fighting the kick in the sub/low bands.\\n4. **Kick + 808 + Reese + Bongo all stacking sub/low** \\u2014 major low-end congestion expected.\\n5. **koto thing (14)** has high low-mid energy (100.6) \\u2014 could be muddying the melodic space.\\n\\n## 2026-04-23 21:00 UTC\\n[Auto-saved on context compaction]\\n\\n# Session Summary: koto (First Render & Analysis)\\n\\n## Project State\\n**Project:** koto | **Status:** First session \\u2014 all 20 tracks + master rendered for the first time\\n\\n### Render Results\\n- **18 of 20 stems rendered successfully** (44.1 kHz, stereo, ~182.5 s duration)\\n- **Master rendered:** koto_Master.wav\\n- **4 failures:** Tracks 18\\u201320 (Insert 18/19/20